    "body": "Reference check (maintainer asked, 2026-11-13): the published documentation of the product CamCraft reimplements describes the setup's WCS Z as the tool direction for that setup (the model is not turned; the operator flips the part). So the reporter followed the workflow that documentation teaches, and \"user error\" in the triage above is too strong: it is a design difference. CamCraft turns the part with Part alignment and now refuses a tilted WCS by name. Whether to keep that or follow the reference is the maintainer's decision, tracked in issue 1542.",
